    "result_text": "There's only one test class in the project, and it passes. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the welcome-notification requirement for the owner-create pipeline.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnqueueWelcomeNotification.java`: reads the saved `Owner` via `@Val` and emits `Welcome owner id={} memberId={}` through the SLF4J logger named `NOTIFY`. It reads the owner after save so the generated id is populated (mirroring how `AuditOwnerCreated` works).\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`: inserted a `notify` step between `audit` and `record`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbors.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreEnqueuesWelcome` (which asserts a `NOTIFY` line contains both the owner id and the memberId) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). Observed log line: `INFO NOTIFY - Welcome owner id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`.",
